</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Results on Long-Horizon Tasks</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ IV-C Results on Long-Horizon Tasks ‣ IV EXPERIMENTS ‣ Cybo-Waiter: A Physical Agentic Framework for Humanoid Whole-Body Locomotion–Manipulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> reports success counts over 10 trials for each task.
Our full system consistently outperforms the ablation <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">W/O Supervisor</span>, improving success from 5/10 to 7/10 on <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tidy-desk</span>, from 6/10 to 8/10 on <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tabletop-sorting</span>, and from 7/10 to 9/10 on <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Bring-me-a-drink</span> (see Figs. <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV EXPERIMENTS ‣ Cybo-Waiter: A Physical Agentic Framework for Humanoid Whole-Body Locomotion–Manipulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ IV EXPERIMENTS ‣ Cybo-Waiter: A Physical Agentic Framework for Humanoid Whole-Body Locomotion–Manipulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for qualitative examples).
These gains highlight the importance of the supervisor in long-horizon execution: by evaluating predicate-based preconditions and success conditions over stable frames, the supervisor reduces premature transitions caused by transient perception noise, detects off-nominal states, and triggers targeted recovery instead of restarting the entire task.
Overall, the results suggest that geometry-grounded monitoring and feedback are critical for maintaining reliable task progression when tasks require repeated object-level actions and extended navigation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
